Clausis trust anchor for online Hermes Agent releases — NOT YET CONFIGURED.

CLAUSIS-PLACEHOLDER-NO-TRUST-ANCHOR

This file must contain the ASCII-armoured OpenPGP public keys of the Hermes
Agent maintainers whose signatures Clausis is willing to accept for an online
release. It ships as a placeholder on purpose: a trust anchor cannot be
generated by the project that consumes it.

While this placeholder is present, `clausis.signing.verify_release` refuses
every online release and the reviewed version bundled in the installation image
stays active. The release gate in `scripts/check_release.py` also stays blocked.

To configure it:

1. Obtain the maintainer keys out of band and verify their fingerprints through
   a second, independent channel — not from the same repository or website that
   serves the releases.
2. Replace this whole file with the armoured public key block(s):
   `gpg --armor --export <FINGERPRINT> > packaging/trust/hermes-maintainers.asc`
3. Record each accepted fingerprint and how it was verified in
   `docs/security/THREAT_MODEL.md`.
4. Re-run the test suite; the placeholder test will then require the real keys
   to parse as an OpenPGP public key block.

Removing this file does not enable updates — a missing trust store fails closed
in exactly the same way.
